@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# Resume Projection Integrity Hardening Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Implement the contract in `specs/state.md` (Checksum-compatible resume projection integrity) as designed in `docs/design/resume_projection_integrity_hardening.md`.
+
+**Architecture:** One pure auditor (`audit_scope`) plus thin call sites: the `resume` command, the structurally-root `WorkflowExecutor`, and the reached-call path of `CallExecutor`. No ID parsing, no retirement/migration evidence, no receipts or caches, schema stays `2.1`.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Python, pytest, `WorkflowStateProjection`, `StateManager`, tmux for the smoke check.
+
+Rules for every task: run from the repository root; no worktrees; narrow selectors first; `pytest --collect-only` on added modules; commit each green task separately; do not touch the protected dirty paths listed in the design plan.
+
+## Task 1: Typed Workflow Lisp provenance (`70a158f`)
+
+- [x] `orchestrator/workflow_lisp/lowering/core.py`: set `provenance.frontend_kind = "workflow_lisp"` before `build_loaded_workflow_bundle`.
+- [x] `orchestrator/workflow_lisp/build.py`: stop overwriting `frontend_kind`; classic-YAML imports keep their provenance object.
+- [x] `CallExecutor._is_workflow_lisp_target` returns `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"` (no `.orc` suffix test).
+- [x] Tests: `tests/test_workflow_lisp_build_artifacts.py`, `tests/test_subworkflow_calls.py`. Tests that exercise bundle reuse in isolation from the Lisp default-resume policy reset `frontend_kind` explicitly.
+
+## Task 2: Classic-YAML import alias duplicates (`65b24ac`)
+
+- [x] `orchestrator/loader_import_aliases.py` composes the YAML node tree and reports duplicates with `line L, column C`; `WorkflowLoader._load_workflow` returns before `build_loaded_workflow_bundle`.
+- [x] Tests in `tests/test_loader_validation.py`: duplicate keys, `<<` in `imports`, repeated sections, merged + explicit section, merge sources each carrying `imports`, single merged section still loads, bundle construction never reached.
+
+## Task 3: Raw state access and safe persistence (`9d567c0`)
+
+- [x] `StateManager.load_raw`, `record_workflow_checksum_mismatch`, `record_resume_projection_integrity_failure`, shared atomic writer; `RunState.from_dict` tolerates malformed `for_each`.
+- [x] Tests in `tests/test_state_manager.py`: JSON diff shows exactly `status`, `error`, `updated_at`; older schemas rejected.
+
+## Task 4: Projection slot index (`13c0aa5`, `ba4916b`)
+
+- [x] `CallBoundaryProjection.import_alias`; `orchestrator/workflow/resume_slots.py`; thin methods on `WorkflowStateProjection`. Declared `repeat_until` maxima are supplied by the auditor (the projection stays golden-compatible).
+- [x] Characterization goldens updated for `import_alias`.
+
+## Task 5: Retry lineage (`402806a`) and auditor (`0bea2e1`)
+
+- [x] `call_frame_lineage.py`, `resume_projection_integrity.py`, `resume_scope_checks.py`; tests in `tests/test_resume_projection_integrity.py` incl. the negative architecture scan.
+
+## Task 6: CLI and executor root audits (`04f639c`)
+
+- [x] `resume.py`: raw read, sticky guard, `audit_scope` before observability/session/process/executor. `executor.py`: `_guard_structural_root_resume` before the prologue; `resume_root_guard.classify_root_checksum`.
+- [x] Characterization tests in `tests/test_resume_command.py` rewritten to the new ordering; envelope, stickiness, race and raw-patch tests added.
+
+## Task 7: Reached-call revalidation and unwrapped propagation (`2a4c763`, `aa764c2`)
+
+- [x] `calls.py` + `call_resume_audit.py`; `loops.py`; `_handle_control_flow` and `finalization.py` for the sticky non-routable rule.
+- [x] Tests: `tests/test_subworkflow_calls.py`, `tests/test_resume_projection_propagation.py`.
+
+## Task 8: Forensic current_step (`8d29e0e`)
+
+- [x] `observability/report.py`, `monitor/classifier.py`, `monitor/messages.py`; tests in `tests/test_observability_report.py`, `tests/test_monitor_classifier.py`.
+
+## Task 9: Verification and status
+
+- [x] Narrow selectors, `pytest --collect-only` on added modules, the full suite (no failure that is not already failing on the seed commit), the tmux smoke check, `wc -l` of new modules, `StateManager.SCHEMA_VERSION == "2.1"`.
+- [x] Status moves to implemented only after Task 9 passes.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A `for_each` nested in a `repeat_until` is rejected by the loader, so that combination has no resume test.
+- The loader rejects `call` steps in root `finally`, so a finalization call step is covered by `FinalizationController` unit tests rather than an end-to-end run.
+- The hand-written legacy states in `tests/` that lacked `current_step.step_id` were updated: the identity is mandatory.
